FEATURE: modal-displayer-verification
DATE: 2026-08-03

================================================================================
CHANGE 1 — New file
================================================================================

OLD_SECTION
(file did not exist)

NEW_SECTION
(new usage guide — see doc/modal-displayer.md for the full text)

Sections: How it works · Quick start · Configuration (full property table,
responsive widths, blur overlay) · API (initialize, close, mainForm, displayForm) ·
Effects · Tall modals · Requirements and gotchas · Complete example.

REASON
`ModalDisplayer` had no documentation. Its behaviour is not discoverable from the
source: it is the only vUX module with no public `show()` method — modals are opened
exclusively by delegated clicks on elements carrying `config.className`, which is
impossible to guess from the constructor's surface. Every `config` property is also
declared write-only via `Object.defineProperties`, so a consumer cannot read back
what is configured and must rely on documentation for defaults and accepted values.

The guide follows the structure of the existing `spa-engine.md` and `data-view.md`
guides for consistency. It documents the trigger-driven model first, then a
minimal working example, then the full configuration table with types and defaults,
and finally the constraints that are easy to get wrong: content must start hidden
with a unique id (the module measures it hidden and restores it by id), only one
modal may be open at a time, `flip` needs an explicit background colour on the
content, and node references into the modal content must not be held across
open/close cycles because the element is cloned into the overlay and restored
afterwards. The "Tall modals" section documents the pin-to-top plus overlay-scroll
behaviour established by the fixes in this change.

