FILES: examples/modal/index.html, examples/modal/main.js, examples/modal/README.md
================================================================================

OLD_SECTION
(files did not exist)

NEW_SECTION
(new runnable example — a demo page, its wiring module, and a README)

REASON
Added to serve two purposes. As documentation it mirrors `examples/spa/`, giving a
working page a consumer can copy from. As verification it is the fixture the
automated browser suite drives: it exercises all four effects, per-trigger widths,
a modal taller than the viewport, all three close routes (close button, Escape,
overlay click) and the open/close callbacks, which is what allowed each defect in
this change to be reproduced before fixing and confirmed after.

Note on `#log { height: 80px; overflow: auto }` in index.html: the on-page log grows
as callbacks fire, and a growing element above the fold triggers Chrome's scroll
anchoring, which shifts the page's scroll offset. That shifted the restored scroll
position by one line height and initially looked like a library bug. Fixing the
log element's height isolates the demo page from the effect; the scroll-restore
behaviour of the module itself was correct.
